      "sequence_position": 2,
      "problem": "How can we best describe the following matrix? \n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}7 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 3 & -1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 5 & 0\\end{aligned}]\n$$",
      "worked_solution": "Notice that $A$ is a matrix for which all entries above the diagonal are $0$'s:\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}7 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 3 & -1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 5 & 0\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nTherefore, it is a lower triangular matrix.\n\nIt is not an upper triangular matrix or a diagonal matrix since there is a non-zero element below the diagonal: ${a}_{21}=3\\ne 0.$",
